course: dictionary
lesson: 8853
title: Shoelace
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A shoelace is a thin string or cord that goes through the holes in a shoe and is tied in a bow to fasten it. You can see and touch a shoelace, so picture your own shoes when you read the word.
explain: Context gives you more clues. «Three breaks in a row she stands near the rope, pretending to tie her shoelace, until the lace is nearly worn through.» The words tie, lace and worn tell you that a shoelace is the string on a shoe, and that it can wear out.
explain: Shoelaces also show you a skill. «Practical skills, such as tying shoelaces, are learned by practising slowly while an adult shows you step by step.» Tying a shoe is something you learn by practising, and loose laces can be dangerous, so it is worth getting it right.
fact: A shoelace is a thin string or cord.
fact: Shoelaces go through holes in a shoe and are tied in a bow to fasten it.
fact: «Undone shoelaces» are loose laces that are not tied, and they can make you trip, especially on stairs.
fact: Loose laces can get caught in escalators or bike chains, so check them before you move off.
fact: Shoelaces can also be used in maths and science to measure curved lines or to make knots.
exercise: What is a shoelace? | A small metal hook for a coat | *A thin string or cord that goes through holes in a shoe | A strap that holds a watch on your wrist
exercise: Why can «undone shoelaces» be dangerous? | They make the shoe look untidy | They make your feet warmer | *They can make you trip, especially on stairs | They stop your shoes from getting wet
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Practical skills, such as tying shoelaces, are learned by practising slowly while an adult shows you step by step.» that means doing something again and again to get better. | shows | *practising | adult | step
test: «She stands near the rope, pretending to tie her shoelace.» What is she pretending to tie? | A knot in a boat | A rope | A bow in her hair | *Her shoelace
test: What does «undone shoelaces» mean? | Laces that are very long | *Laces that have come loose and are not tied | Laces tied in a double knot | Laces that are new and shiny
exam: Why is learning to tie your shoelaces important? | It makes you run faster than everyone else | It keeps your feet warm in winter | *It stops laces coming undone and catching you, so you stay safe | It makes your shoes lighter
